<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8"/>
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1.0"/>
<title>WebDev Mastery — HTML · CSS · JS · React</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:wght@400;600&family=Outfit:wght@400;500;600;700;800&display=swap" rel="stylesheet"/>
<style>
*,*::before,*::after{box-sizing:border-box;margin:0;padding:0}
:root{
  --bg:#07090f;--surface:#0d1117;--card:#111827;--border:#1f2937;
  --html:#f97316;--css:#3b82f6;--js:#eab308;--react:#06b6d4;--ml:#10b981;
  --green:#22c55e;--red:#ef4444;--purple:#a855f7;
  --text:#f1f5f9;--muted:#64748b;--dim:#1e293b;
  --mono:'IBM Plex Mono',monospace;--sans:'Outfit',sans-serif;
  --accent:var(--html);
}
html,body{height:100%;background:var(--bg);color:var(--text);font-family:var(--sans);overflow:hidden}
#app{display:flex;flex-direction:column;height:100vh}
::-webkit-scrollbar{width:4px;height:4px}
::-webkit-scrollbar-track{background:transparent}
::-webkit-scrollbar-thumb{background:#1f2937;border-radius:4px}
button{cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--sans)}
input,textarea,select{font-family:var(--sans)}

/* TOPBAR */
#topbar{
  background:var(--surface);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:0 16px;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:0;flex-shrink:0;height:52px;
}
.track-tab{
  display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;padding:0 18px;height:52px;
  border:none;background:transparent;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;
  font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;border-bottom:3px solid transparent;
  transition:all .2s;white-space:nowrap;font-family:var(--sans);
}
.track-tab:hover{color:var(--text)}
.track-tab.active{color:var(--text);border-bottom-color:var(--accent)}
.track-tab .dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;flex-shrink:0}
#topbar-right{margin-left:auto;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px}
.progress-pill{
  background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:99px;
  padding:4px 12px;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;
}
.progress-bar{width:60px;height:4px;background:var(--border);border-radius:99px;overflow:hidden}
.progress-fill{height:100%;border-radius:99px;transition:width .4s;background:var(--accent)}

/* MAIN LAYOUT */
#main{display:flex;flex:1;overflow:hidden}

/* SIDEBAR — lesson list */
#sidebar{
  width:200px;background:var(--surface);border-right:1px solid var(--border);
  overflow-y:auto;flex-shrink:0;
}
.lesson-btn{
  width:100%;background:transparent;border:none;border-left:3px solid transparent;
  border-right:none;border-top:none;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:10px 12px;text-align:left;cursor:pointer;
  display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;transition:all .15s;
}
.lesson-btn:hover{background:var(--card)}
.lesson-btn.active{background:var(--card);border-left-color:var(--accent)}
.lesson-btn .l-num{font-size:10px;color:var(--muted);flex-shrink:0;width:18px}
.lesson-btn .l-title{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:500;line-height:1.3}
.lesson-btn.active .l-title{color:var(--text);font-weight:700}
.lesson-btn .l-done{font-size:11px;flex-shrink:0}

/* CENTER — lesson content */
#center{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;overflow:hidden;min-width:0}

/* lesson header */
#lesson-header{
  background:var(--surface);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  padding:13px 18px;flex-shrink:0;
}
#lesson-title{font-size:17px;font-weight:800;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:4px}
#lesson-concept{
  background:var(--bg);border-left:3px solid var(--accent);border-radius:0 6px 6px 0;
  padding:7px 12px;font-size:12px;color:#94a3b8;
}
#lesson-concept b{color:var(--accent)}

/* tabs */
#tabs{
  display:flex;background:var(--surface);border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);flex-shrink:0;
}
.tab-btn{
  background:transparent;border:none;border-bottom:2px solid transparent;
  padding:9px 16px;color:var(--muted);font-size:12px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer;
  font-family:var(--sans);transition:all .15s;
}
.tab-btn.active{color:var(--text);background:var(--bg);border-bottom-color:var(--accent)}

/* content area */
#content{flex:1;overflow-y:auto;padding:18px}

/* code block */
.code-block{
  background:#050810;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;
  padding:16px 18px;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.8;
  color:#cbd5e1;white-space:pre-wrap;word-break:break-word;margin-bottom:12px;
}
.code-block .cm{color:#7dd3fc} /* keyword */
.code-block .cv{color:#86efac} /* value/string */
.code-block .cc{color:#475569;font-style:italic} /* comment */
.code-block .ct{color:#fda4af} /* tag */
.code-block .cp{color:#c4b5fd} /* property */
.code-block .cf{color:#fbbf24} /* function */

/* theory sections */
.section-title{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;color:var(--accent);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;margin:18px 0 8px}
.section-title:first-child{margin-top:0}
.theory-text{font-size:13px;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.7;margin-bottom:10px}

/* demo box */
.demo-box{
  background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;
}
.demo-header{
  background:var(--bg);padding:8px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
  font-size:10px;color:var(--muted);display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;
}
.demo-dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%}
.demo-body{padding:16px}

/* RIGHT — sidebox */
#sidebox{
  width:240px;background:var(--surface);border-left:1px solid var(--border);
  overflow-y:auto;flex-shrink:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;
}
#sidebox-header{
  padding:12px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);font-size:11px;
  font-weight:700;color:var(--muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.08em;
  flex-shrink:0;
}
.tip-card{
  margin:10px;background:var(--card);border:1px solid var(--border);
  border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;
}
.tip-card-head{
  padding:8px 12px;font-size:10px;font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;
  text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);
}
.tip-card-body{padding:10px 12px;font-size:11.5px;color:#94a3b8;line-height:1.65}
.tip-card-body code{
  font-family:var(--mono);background:#050810;padding:1px 5px;border-radius:3px;
  font-size:10.5px;color:#7dd3fc;
}
.tip-tag{
  display:inline-block;padding:1px 7px;border-radius:99px;font-size:10px;
  font-weight:700;margin:2px 2px 0 0;
}
.link-tip{
  margin:6px 12px;padding:8px 10px;background:var(--dim);border-radius:6px;
  font-size:11px;color:#64748b;border-left:2px solid var(--accent);cursor:pointer;
  transition:all .15s;
}
.link-tip:hover{color:var(--text);background:var(--card)}
.link-tip b{color:var(--accent)}

/* DEMO interactive elements */
.d-btn{
  background:var(--accent);color:#fff;border:none;border-radius:7px;
  padding:8px 18px;font-weight:700;font-size:13px;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--sans);
  transition:opacity .15s;
}
.d-btn:hover{opacity:.85}
.d-btn.secondary{background:var(--dim);color:#94a3b8}
.d-input{
  background:#050810;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:7px;
  padding:8px 12px;color:var(--text);font-size:13px;width:100%;margin-bottom:8px;outline:none;
  font-family:var(--sans);
}
.d-input:focus{border-color:var(--accent)}

/* progress dots */
#pdots{display:flex;gap:4px;align-items:center}
.pdot{width:6px;height:6px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--border);cursor:pointer;transition:all .2s}
.pdot.cur{background:var(--accent);width:18px;border-radius:4px}
.pdot.done{background:var(--green)}

/* footer */
#footer{
  background:var(--surface);border-top:1px solid var(--border);padding:10px 18px;
  display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;flex-shrink:0;
}
.f-btn{
  background:var(--dim);color:#94a3b8;border:none;border-radius:7px;
  padding:8px 18px;font-weight:700;font-size:12px;cursor:pointer;font-family:var(--sans);
}
.f-btn:disabled{opacity:.3;cursor:not-allowed}
.f-btn.primary{background:var(--accent);color:#fff}

@keyframes spin{to{transform:rotate(360deg)}}
@keyframes fadeUp{from{opacity:0;transform:translateY(8px)}to{opacity:1;transform:translateY(0)}}
.fade{animation:fadeUp .2s ease forwards}

/* callout box */
.callout{
  border-radius:8px;padding:10px 14px;margin-bottom:12px;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6;
}
.callout.warn{background:#451a0322;border:1px solid #f9731633;color:#fdba74}
.callout.info{background:#0c1a3322;border:1px solid #3b82f633;color:#93c5fd}
.callout.success{background:#052e1622;border:1px solid #22c55e33;color:#86efac}

/* compare table */
.compare{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12px;margin-bottom:12px}
.compare th{background:var(--dim);padding:7px 12px;text-align:left;font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;color:var(--muted)}
.compare td{padding:7px 12px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--border);color:#94a3b8;vertical-align:top}
.compare td:first-child{color:var(--text);font-weight:600;font-family:var(--mono);font-size:11px}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="app">
  <div id="topbar">
    <button class="track-tab active" data-track="html" onclick="switchTrack('html')">
      <span class="dot" style="background:#f97316"></span> HTML
    </button>
    <button class="track-tab" data-track="css" onclick="switchTrack('css')">
      <span class="dot" style="background:#3b82f6"></span> CSS
    </button>
    <button class="track-tab" data-track="js" onclick="switchTrack('js')">
      <span class="dot" style="background:#eab308"></span> JavaScript
    </button>
    <button class="track-tab" data-track="react" onclick="switchTrack('react')">
      <span class="dot" style="background:#06b6d4"></span> React
    </button>
    <button class="track-tab" data-track="ml" onclick="switchTrack('ml')">
      <span class="dot" style="background:#10b981"></span> ML
    </button>
    <div id="topbar-right">
      <div class="progress-pill">
        <span id="prog-text">0 / 0</span>
        <div class="progress-bar"><div class="progress-fill" id="prog-fill" style="width:0%"></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div id="main">
    <div id="sidebar" id="sidebar"></div>

    <div id="center">
      <div id="lesson-header">
        <div id="lesson-title">Loading...</div>
        <div id="lesson-concept"></div>
      </div>
      <div id="tabs">
        <button class="tab-btn active" onclick="switchTab('learn')">📖 Learn</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab('demo')">🎮 Demo</button>
        <button class="tab-btn" onclick="switchTab('practice')">✏️ Practice</button>
      </div>
      <div id="content" class="fade"></div>
      <div id="footer">
        <button class="f-btn" id="btn-prev" onclick="navigate(-1)">← Previous</button>
        <div id="pdots"></div>
        <button class="f-btn primary" id="btn-next" onclick="navigate(1)">Next →</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div id="sidebox">
      <div id="sidebox-header">💡 Tips & Connections</div>
      <div id="sidebox-body"></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
// COURSE DATA
// ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
const TRACKS = {
  html: {
    color: '#f97316',
    label: 'HTML',
    lessons: [
      {
        id:'h1', emoji:'🏗️', title:'What is HTML?',
        concept:'HTML is the <b>skeleton</b> of every webpage — it defines structure, not looks.',
        learn: `<div class="section-title">What HTML Does</div>
<p class="theory-text">HTML (HyperText Markup Language) gives a webpage its <strong>structure</strong>. Think of building a house — HTML is the walls, floors, and rooms. CSS paints it, JavaScript makes it move.</p>
<div class="callout info">Every website you've ever visited — Google, YouTube, Instagram — starts with an HTML file.</div>
<div class="section-title">How HTML Works</div>
<p class="theory-text">HTML uses <strong>tags</strong> — words in angle brackets — to label content. Most tags come in pairs: an opening tag and a closing tag.</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="ct">&lt;h1&gt;</span>I am a heading<span class="ct">&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;p&gt;</span>I am a paragraph.<span class="ct">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;img</span> <span class="cp">src</span>=<span class="cv">"photo.jpg"</span> <span class="ct">/&gt;</span>  <span class="cc">← self-closing, no pair needed</span></div>
<div class="section-title">The Basic Page Structure</div>
<div class="code-block"><span class="ct">&lt;!DOCTYPE html&gt;</span>              <span class="cc">← tells browser: this is HTML5</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;html</span> <span class="cp">lang</span>=<span class="cv">"en"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>               <span class="cc">← root element</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;head&gt;</span>                       <span class="cc">← invisible info (title, styles)</span>
    <span class="ct">&lt;title&gt;</span>My Page<span class="ct">&lt;/title&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;/head&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;body&gt;</span>                       <span class="cc">← everything visible goes here</span>
    <span class="ct">&lt;h1&gt;</span>Hello World!<span class="ct">&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
    <span class="ct">&lt;p&gt;</span>My first webpage.<span class="ct">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;/body&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;/html&gt;</span></div>`,
        demo: 'html_structure',
        practice: {q:'What tag makes a large heading?', a:'h1', hint:'It\'s written as &lt;h1&gt;'},
        tips: [
          {track:'css', color:'#3b82f6', title:'CSS Connection', body:'HTML gives structure. CSS gives style. You\'ll link a CSS file in the <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> with <code>&lt;link rel="stylesheet"&gt;</code>'},
          {track:'js', color:'#eab308', title:'JS Connection', body:'JavaScript finds HTML elements using <code>document.getElementById()</code> or <code>querySelector()</code> to make them interactive.'},
          {type:'tip', title:'Remember', body:'If you forget to close a tag, the browser will try to guess — but your layout will break in weird ways. Always close your tags!'},
        ]
      },
      {
        id:'h2', emoji:'📝', title:'Text & Headings',
        concept:'Headings h1–h6 create <b>hierarchy</b>. Paragraphs hold body text.',
        learn: `<div class="section-title">Heading Tags</div>
<p class="theory-text">There are 6 heading levels. Use them for hierarchy — like a document outline. h1 is the biggest (page title), h6 is smallest.</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="ct">&lt;h1&gt;</span>Page Title — use once per page<span class="ct">&lt;/h1&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;h2&gt;</span>Main Section<span class="ct">&lt;/h2&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;h3&gt;</span>Sub-section<span class="ct">&lt;/h3&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;h4&gt;</span>Sub-sub-section<span class="ct">&lt;/h4&gt;</span></div>
<div class="section-title">Text Tags</div>
<div class="code-block"><span class="ct">&lt;p&gt;</span>A paragraph. Main block of text.<span class="ct">&lt;/p&gt;</span>

<span class="ct">&lt;strong&gt;</span>Bold — important text<span class="ct">&lt;/strong&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;em&gt;</span>Italic — emphasized text<span class="ct">&lt;/em&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;br</span> <span class="ct">/&gt;</span>  <span class="cc">← line break (no closing tag)</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;hr</span> <span class="ct">/&gt;</span>  <span class="cc">← horizontal line divider</span>

<span class="ct">&lt;span</span> <span class="cp">style</span>=<span class="cv">"color:red"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>Inline colored text<span class="ct">&lt;/span&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;small&gt;</span>Fine print<span class="ct">&lt;/small&gt;</span></div>
<div class="section-title">Lists</div>
<div class="code-block"><span class="cc">/* Unordered (bullet) list */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;ul&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;li&gt;</span>Apples<span class="ct">&lt;/li&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;li&gt;</span>Bananas<span class="ct">&lt;/li&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;/ul&gt;</span>

<span class="cc">/* Ordered (numbered) list */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;ol&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;li&gt;</span>Step one<span class="ct">&lt;/li&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;li&gt;</span>Step two<span class="ct">&lt;/li&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;/ol&gt;</span></div>`,
        demo: 'html_text',
        practice: {q:'Write a tag to make text bold and important', a:'strong', hint:'Not just visual — use the semantic tag for "important"'},
        tips: [
          {track:'css', color:'#3b82f6', title:'Styling Text', body:'In CSS, you\'ll use <code>font-size</code>, <code>color</code>, <code>font-weight</code>, <code>font-family</code> to style these tags.'},
          {type:'tip', title:'Semantic vs Visual', body:'Use <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> not <code>&lt;b&gt;</code> for bold. They look the same but <code>&lt;strong&gt;</code> tells screen readers it\'s important.'},
        ]
      },
      {
        id:'h3', emoji:'🔗', title:'Links & Images',
        concept:'<b>Attributes</b> add extra info to tags — like href for links and src for images.',
        learn: `<div class="section-title">Links — &lt;a&gt; tag</div>
<p class="theory-text">The <code>&lt;a&gt;</code> (anchor) tag creates clickable links. The <code>href</code> attribute tells it WHERE to go.</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="cc">/* Link to another website */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;a</span> <span class="cp">href</span>=<span class="cv">"https://google.com"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>Go to Google<span class="ct">&lt;/a&gt;</span>

<span class="cc">/* Open in a new tab */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;a</span> <span class="cp">href</span>=<span class="cv">"https://google.com"</span> <span class="cp">target</span>=<span class="cv">"_blank"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>New Tab<span class="ct">&lt;/a&gt;</span>

<span class="cc">/* Link to a section on same page */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;a</span> <span class="cp">href</span>=<span class="cv">"#contact"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>Jump to Contact<span class="ct">&lt;/a&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;section</span> <span class="cp">id</span>=<span class="cv">"contact"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>...<span class="ct">&lt;/section&gt;</span>

<span class="cc">/* Email link */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;a</span> <span class="cp">href</span>=<span class="cv">"mailto:me@example.com"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>Email Me<span class="ct">&lt;/a&gt;</span></div>
<div class="section-title">Images — &lt;img&gt; tag</div>
<div class="code-block"><span class="cc">/* Self-closing — no &lt;/img&gt; needed */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;img</span>
  <span class="cp">src</span>=<span class="cv">"photo.jpg"</span>          <span class="cc">← file path or URL</span>
  <span class="cp">alt</span>=<span class="cv">"A scenic mountain"</span>  <span class="cc">← description (required!)</span>
  <span class="cp">width</span>=<span class="cv">"300"</span>            <span class="cc">← in pixels</span>
<span class="ct">/&gt;</span>

<span class="cc">/* Image from the web */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;img</span> <span class="cp">src</span>=<span class="cv">"https://example.com/img.jpg"</span> <span class="cp">alt</span>=<span class="cv">"desc"</span> <span class="ct">/&gt;</span>

<span class="cc">/* Clickable image = wrap img in a tag */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;a</span> <span class="cp">href</span>=<span class="cv">"https://site.com"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;img</span> <span class="cp">src</span>=<span class="cv">"logo.png"</span> <span class="cp">alt</span>=<span class="cv">"Logo"</span> <span class="ct">/&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;/a&gt;</span></div>`,
        demo: 'html_links',
        practice: {q:'What attribute defines where a link goes?', a:'href', hint:'It stands for Hypertext REFerence'},
        tips: [
          {type:'tip', title:'Alt text matters', body:'Always write descriptive <code>alt</code> text on images. Screen readers use it for visually impaired users, and it shows if the image fails to load.'},
          {track:'js', color:'#eab308', title:'JS: Click Events', body:'In JavaScript, you can add <code>onclick</code> to any element, not just links — to run code when clicked.'},
        ]
      },
      {
        id:'h4', emoji:'📦', title:'Divs, Sections & Layout',
        concept:'<b>div</b> and semantic tags are containers — they group content for styling & layout.',
        learn: `<div class="section-title">The div — Your Main Container</div>
<p class="theory-text"><code>&lt;div&gt;</code> is a generic box. It has no visual meaning — it's just a container you can style with CSS. Most layouts are built from divs.</p>
<div class="code-block"><span class="ct">&lt;div</span> <span class="cp">class</span>=<span class="cv">"card"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;h2&gt;</span>Card Title<span class="ct">&lt;/h2&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;p&gt;</span>Card content here<span class="ct">&lt;/p&gt;</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;/div&gt;</span>

<span class="cc">/* Multiple divs side by side (via CSS) */</span>
<span class="ct">&lt;div</span> <span class="cp">class</span>=<span class="cv">"container"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;div</span> <span class="cp">class</span>=<span class="cv">"col"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>Left<span class="ct">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
  <span class="ct">&lt;div</span> <span class="cp">class</span>=<span class="cv">"col"</span><span class="ct">&gt;</span>Right<span class="ct">&lt;/div&gt;</span>
